---
/** D14. /guides/best-action-manhwa — see src/components/BestManhwa.astro. */
export const prerender = true
import BestManhwa from '../../components/BestManhwa.astro'
---

<BestManhwa
  slug="best-action-manhwa"
  genre="Action"
  keywords={['best action manhwa', 'action manhwa', 'best action webtoons', 'action manhwa to read', 'top action manhwa']}
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Action manhwa are behind most of the genre's big crossover hits: hunters clearing dungeons, returners who
      go back in time to fix their mistakes, martial artists climbing the murim, and regressors who remember how
      the world ends. Full-colour vertical scrolling suits fight scenes, and the best of them move like a storyboard.
    </p>
    <p>
      This list keeps to action manhwa you can read on an official platform, ranked by what readers scored them.
      Each title links to its page, with every official platform and whether you can start free.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Reading action manhwa on the official apps</h2>
  <p>
    Most of the big action series run on WEBTOON, Tapas and Tappytoon in English, and on Naver Webtoon and
    KakaoPage in Korean, where new chapters usually appear first. WEBTOON and Tapas let you read most of a series
    free and charge only for the newest chapters, which makes them the cheapest way to catch up on a long action
    series. Several of the titles here also have an anime adaptation; their title pages link to it, with the
    services that stream it.
  </p>
</BestManhwa>
